  ],
  "notes": "FORMS:\n{引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぐ (to take over, to succeed) → nominalized form\n{引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぐ (godan) - to take over, to succeed to\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ{書|しょ} (handover document)\n- {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ{資料|しりょう} (handover materials)\n- {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ{期間|きかん} (handover period)\n- {業務|ぎょうむ}{引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ (work handover)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {申|もう}し{送|おく}り (briefing, passing on information)\n- {後任|こうにん} (successor)\n- {前任|ぜんにん} (predecessor)\n\nWORKPLACE USAGE:\nProper {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ is considered essential in Japanese workplaces. Leaving without adequate handover is seen as irresponsible. Common when changing jobs, transferring departments, or retiring.",
